---
import Prose from '../components/Prose.astro';
import Table from '../components/Table.astro';
import CustomFlow from '../components/gestures/CustomFlow.svelte';
import InAList from '../components/gestures/InAList.svelte';
import Swipes from '../components/gestures/Swipes.svelte';
import Taps from '../components/gestures/Taps.svelte';
import DocsLayout from '../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
---

<DocsLayout slug="gestures">
  <p class="text-base text-muted">
    Describe a gesture as a string, like <code>'double-tap'</code> or <code>'tap tap hold+swipe-left'</code>, and get a
    callback. Touch, pen and mouse. Scrolling stays native wherever it can.
  </p>
  <Taps client:visible={{ rootMargin: '300px' }} />
  <InAList client:visible={{ rootMargin: '300px' }} />
  <CustomFlow client:visible={{ rootMargin: '300px' }} />
  <Swipes client:visible={{ rootMargin: '300px' }} />
  <section id="patterns">
    <h2>Patterns</h2>
    <Prose
      text="A pattern is a list of presses separated by spaces (or an array). Each press is a combination of tokens joined with `+`, in the order they happen while the finger is down."
    />
    <Table
      head={['Token', 'Alias', 'Description']}
      rows={[
        ['tap', '', 'Pressed and released without holding or moving more than `slop`.'],
        ['hold', 'long-press', 'Held still for `holdTime`.'],
        ['swipe-up', '', 'Moved `swipeDistance` up. Also `swipe-down`, `swipe-left`, `swipe-right`.'],
        ['swipe', '', 'Any swipe direction.'],
        ['tap tap', 'double-tap', 'Two presses within `interval`.'],
        ['tap tap tap', 'triple-tap', ''],
      ]}
    />
    <Prose
      text="A gesture fires as soon as no other bound pattern can still extend it: right away, or once the next press goes elsewhere, or after `interval`. A press that doesn't fit restarts the sequence from that press, and `hold` only counts when a bound pattern uses it. Handlers get `{ gesture, steps, direction, target, event }`."
    />
  </section>
  <section id="options">
    <h2>Options</h2>
    <Table
      head={['Option', 'Default', 'Description']}
      rows={[
        ['target', '', 'Element that receives the presses. Element or selector.'],
        ['gestures', '', "Initial bindings, keyed by pattern: `{ 'double-tap': fn }`."],
        [
          'holdTime',
          '500',
          'ms a press must be held still to count as `hold`. Only recognized when a pattern uses `hold`.',
        ],
        ['interval', '300', 'Max ms between releasing and pressing again within a sequence.'],
        ['swipeDistance', '50', 'px a press must move in one direction to count as a swipe.'],
        ['slop', '10', 'px a press may move and still be a `tap` or `hold`.'],
        ['mouse', 'true', 'Recognize mouse presses (primary button). Touch and pen always work.'],
        ['disabled', 'false', 'Ignore input.'],
      ]}
    />
    <h3>Instance</h3>
    <p>
      <code>on(pattern, handler)</code> (returns <code>off</code>), <code>reset()</code>,
      <code>setOptions(partial)</code>, <code>getState()</code> → <code>{'{ pressed, steps }'}</code>,
      <code>subscribe(fn)</code>, <code>destroy()</code>.
    </p>
    <h3>Browser defaults</h3>
    <Prose
      text="Derived from the bindings and restored on `destroy()`: `touch-action` blocks scrolling only on the axes that swipe from the start of a press, and is `manipulation` (no double-tap zoom) for multi-press patterns. With `hold` bound, the iOS callout, text selection and Android's context menu are off. A mouse hold or swipe that fires doesn't also click. A mouse swipe can still select text unless `hold` is bound (or you set `user-select: none`). Patterns that can never match throw when bound: `hold` must be first in a press and only once, and the same direction twice in a row is one swipe. An exception in a handler or subscriber is reported with `reportError` and doesn't affect the others."
    />
    <h3>Styling hooks</h3>
    <Table
      head={['Hook', 'On', 'Description']}
      rows={[
        ['data-zupf-gestures', 'target', 'Set while attached.'],
        ['data-pressed', 'target', 'A press is in progress.'],
        ['data-holding', 'target', 'The press became a `hold`.'],
      ]}
    />
  </section>
</DocsLayout>
